  "verbalization": "Isoswinholide B appears to interact with Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6 through multiple distinct pathways. The first pathway links Isoswinholide B to U-87 MG, which is targeted by (2S)-3',4'-Dihydroxy-6,7-Dimethoxyflavan, and this compound in turn targets the enzyme. The second pathway connects Isoswinholide B to Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13, which is targeted by Phytolaccoside B, and Phytolaccoside B also targets the same enzyme. The third pathway links Isoswinholide B to Serine/threonine-protein kinase Nek5, which is targeted by Phytolaccoside B, and again targets the same enzyme. These findings suggest that Isoswinholide B may act through different molecular mechanisms to inhibit the enzyme, potentially through distinct upstream targets. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Isoswinholide B and the enzyme, though the exact mode of action remains to be elucidated. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further validation through independent experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the biological relevance.",
